  "result": "Perfect! All 52 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Summary of additions:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Two new calculation functions:\n   - `lineTotal(line)` \u2014 Returns `ok(qty \u00d7 unitPrice)` or `fail('LINE_INVALID')` if the line is malformed\n   - `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 Returns `ok({ subtotal, total })` where subtotal is the sum of all line totals and total equals subtotal for now (VAT and discounts come later), or `fail('INVOICE_INVALID')` if the invoice structure is invalid\n\n2. **src/errors.js** \u2014 Two new error codes:\n   - `LINE_INVALID`: \"Line must have a positive integer quantity and a unit price.\"\n   - `INVOICE_INVALID`: \"Invoice must have a valid lines array.\"\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 19 new tests covering:\n   - Happy paths with various quantities and unit prices\n   - All validation edge cases (missing properties, invalid types, negative values)\n   - Correct calculation of totals\n   - Error propagation from lineTotal to invoiceTotals\n   - Large invoices with many lines\n\nAll calculations use integers (cents) as required by the house rules.",
